{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-3012"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Building of pleasure and sporting boats"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "3012"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :boat-building/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :occupant-safety :boater-safety]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :boat-building-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :eda :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "BoatAdvisor ⊣ Boat Building Plant Operations Governor,
 langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant
 OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor for pleasure and sporting boat
 building (hull-molding/rigging/final-assembly/water-test lines
 producing finished sailboats, motorboats, personal watercraft and
 other pleasure/sporting craft) -- not direct hull-molding/rigging/
 final-assembly/water-test-equipment control authority and not a
 marine-classification / seaworthiness-certification authority. Four
 ops (`:log-production-batch` / `:schedule-maintenance` /
 `:flag-safety-concern` / `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect
 :propose` only. Twelve concrete governor checks elaborate this
 blueprint's four HARD invariants: propose-only effect, closed op
 allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct hull-molding/
 rigging/final-assembly/water-test-equipment control), permanent
 equipment-actuate block, permanent marine-classification/
 seaworthiness-certification-authority block (this actor never
 self-issues an ISO 12217 stability-and-buoyancy assessment or a CE
 Recreational Craft Directive conformity mark), independent equipment
 verification/registration before maintenance scheduling, independent
 batch verification/registration before shipment coordination,
 independent shipment-quantity recompute against the batch's own
 logged production quantity, double-schedule guard, product-category
 validation, hull-length plausibility validation, and hull-defect-
 rate plausibility validation. Safety-concern flagging (hull-
 integrity-defect/buoyancy-test-failure/materials-safety) ALWAYS
 escalates to a human plant supervisor; `:log-production-batch` is
 the only op eligible to auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when
 governor-clean."}
